# The shape NEXT to defect 037's repair, pinned so the repair cannot widen into
# it (panel 152 R2; measured 2026-09-15 before and after the repair landed).
#
# The compiler now supplies `struct` in front of a handle's tag when clang
# refuses the bare word with *must use 'struct' tag to refer to type 'X'*. That
# message is produced only when X names a struct tag of exactly that spelling.
# A MISSPELLED tag gets a different sentence — *unknown type name 'addrinfoo'*
# — and this file is the witness that the compiler keeps the two apart: the
# misspelling stays refused, on the author's own line, and is never dressed as
# `struct addrinfoo *`, which C would accept as a brand-new empty type and
# clang would never mention again. That silent acceptance is the reason panel
# 152 refused a one-bit probe: `struct nosuchtype *p;` compiles at exit 0.
#
# This file must NOT compile. Its emission is blessed with the misspelled word
# written bare, which is what the author wrote.

extern "netdb.h"
    record AI tag addrinfoo  #~ ffi_unknown_name
    function freeaddrinfo(ai: AI consumes)

function main()
    print(0)
